    "scope": "W kernel only: complete passive normalized grammar; OR within known value groups, AND across groups and SRX predicates; full supplied adjacency and detached field projection. No CLI, public page, live project coverage, evaluation currency or computed verification result is claimed. Current provider gaps fail explicitly, including for empty input. The four requirements remain partial. R rejects unknown or non-normalized envelope fields, incorrect SRX content hashes, unsupported operators and invalid alternatives in known filter vocabularies. Invalid known stored status fields anywhere in the supplied inventory block selection. Computed verification projection requires its actual provider even with no matches; passive nested extension values remain data. No current verification aggregation is claimed. C extracts normalization and stored-field projection into private pure helpers at the original call sites. Public classes and module identities, existing W/R cases, errors, bindings and provider boundaries remain unchanged. 8.c.W now executes the full_text group with literal NFC/casefold search; repeated terms are OR and compose with the existing groups/SRX by AND. Its former missing-provider empty-input case now requires the exact empty selection; other provider failures remain unchanged. 8.c.R binds every search observation to an exact SourceRelations record, retaining original bytes and raw SHA-256 separately from immutable normalized copies. Repeated queries rebuild current copies even for the same ID; canonically equivalent sources and alternative JSON encodings retain distinct source bindings. Actual available locale switches occur only in an isolated child process, with exact hit, projection and byte oracles; C is mandatory, additional installed locales are covered without a cross-platform completeness claim. All prior W expectations remain unchanged. 8.c.C moves the identical field-selection/normalization function into a private pure working-copy module. SearchText and literal matching retain their module identity and source ownership behavior. All W/R tests and IDs remain unchanged; an AST proof binds the moved function and remaining source module to the authoritative R Result. 8.d.W adds query_records and an owned QueryPage with exactly items/total/offset/limit/returned/truncated. All supplied-inventory filters execute before exact counting, full scalar sorting and pagination. Missing/null/Boolean/numeric/string precedence, NFC UTF-8 string order, mixed directions and final ascending ID tie-breaking have independent result oracles. Projection never removes sort operands. Object/array sort values fail before pagination, and computed verification sorting requires the actual provider even for empty input. Source bytes, query/input bindings and all existing selection behavior remain unchanged. The synchronous kernel is in-memory; R/C continuation and M6 spooling, public CLI/live-project delivery and current semantic providers remain open."
